## 1. Eight Distinct Project Concepts (Section 6 Requirement)

To avoid generating superficial variations of the same app, we engineered **8 structurally distinct project concepts** addressing different failure points identified in our research.

---

### Concept 1: **Pragnya KisanPulse** — Counterfactual Yield & Input-Timing Optimizer
1. **Project Identity:**
   * **One-Line Description:** Zero-hardware satellite-soil-weather decision engine that predicts uncertainty-bounded yield (`P10–P90`) and simulates 7-day "What-If" irrigation and urea timing scenarios to prevent weather-induced waste.
   * **Main Objective:** Maximize net farmer return per acre (`Yield Value − Input Waste`) during the critical mid-season window (Days 30–90).
   * **Primary Target User:** Smallholder irrigated/rainfed farmers (1–5 acres) and FPOs in Telangana, Andhra Pradesh, Odisha, Punjab, and Haryana.
2. **Real-World Problem:** Farmers lose **55–70% of applied urea** to leaching/runoff ([PIB 2026](https://www.pib.gov.in/PressReleasePage.aspx?PRID=2237709)) and over-extract groundwater ([Earth5R / CGWB 2025](https://earth5r.org/groundwater-depletion-india/)) because they apply inputs on fixed routines right before unseasonal rain or without checking canopy moisture (`NDMI`).
3. **Proposed Solution & User Journey:** Farmer drops a GPS pin or enters an [AgriStack Farmer ID](https://agristack.gov.in/) → System fetches 10m Sentinel-2 (`SAVI`, `NDMI`, `NDRE`), Sentinel-1 SAR (`VV/VH`), village Soil Health Card baselines, and 7-day forecast → Outputs calibrated yield range (`P10/P50/P90`) + compares 3 input timing choices (*Apply Today* vs. *Delay 4 Days* vs. *Split Dose*) → Sends 15-second Telugu/Hindi voice advisory.
4. **Innovation:** Replaces static yield prediction with a **zero-hardware counterfactual simulator** combining the 81-day SAVI early-prediction window ([IJISAE](https://ijisae.org/index.php/IJISAE/article/view/2326)) and rain-leaching loss physics.
5. **AI Involvement:** CatBoost/XGBoost with **Conformal Quantile Regression** (yield distribution), Temporal Savitzky-Golay + SAR-Optical fusion (satellite time-series imputation), Multi-Objective Counterfactual Search (action ranking), and LLM/TTS strictly for translating structured output into vernacular voice.
6. **Data Requirements:** [UPAg District APY](https://upag.gov.in/dash-reports/desdistrictwisecompletedatasetreport), [Copernicus Sentinel-1/2](https://dataspace.copernicus.eu/), NASA POWER / Open-Meteo 7-day forecast, [ISRIC SoilGrids](https://un-spider.org/sites/default/files/GeoAI%20Compendium%202026.pdf) + SHC district summaries.
7. **Technical Feasibility (15 Days):** **High.** All APIs are public and free; tabular + temporal feature fusion trains in minutes on a laptop CPU/GPU.
8. **User Benefits:** Saves 25–35% urea loss during wet spells and 15–25% irrigation water while protecting 8–12% yield from waterlogging/stress (under stated simulation assumptions).
9. **Limitations:** 10m pixel resolution can blur sub-0.2-acre plots; requires disaggregating district yield labels using pixel SAVI anomalies.
10. **Demonstration Potential:** Live interactive map of real farms in Khammam (Telangana), Kakinada (AP), and Ludhiana (Punjab) with interactive sliders to simulate incoming storms and watch the AI shift urea/irrigation timing and calculate ₹ saved.

