### Concept 2: **SAR-Shield** — Cloud-Proof Monsoon & Cyclone Pre-Harvest Salvage Engine
1. **Project Identity:**
   * **One-Line Description:** All-weather C-band SAR + synoptic weather risk engine that predicts cyclone submergence and crop lodging impact 5 days ahead and recommends pre-storm harvest or drainage actions.
   * **Main Objective:** Minimize catastrophic pre-harvest crop loss during October–November cyclones and monsoon floods.
   * **Primary Target User:** Coastal paddy and banana/horticulture farmers and FPOs in Andhra Pradesh, Odisha, and Tamil Nadu.
2. **Real-World Problem:** Cyclones **Arnab and Murasu** damaged **4.61 lakh hectares** in AP in Nov 2026 ([DD News](https://ddnews.gov.in/en/cyclones-arnab-murasu-damage-crops-across-4-61-lakh-hectares-in-andhra-pradesh/)), catching ready-to-harvest paddy fields where optical satellites were blinded by storm clouds.
3. **Proposed Solution:** Combines [Sentinel-1 SAR](https://dataspace.copernicus.eu/data-collections/copernicus-sentinel-missions/sentinel-1) backscatter (`VH/VV` ratio + flood mask), Digital Elevation Model (DEM) topographic wetness index, and cyclone wind/rain tracks to compare *Early Harvest at 85% Maturity* vs. *Wait & Risk Lodging*.
4. **Innovation:** Uses radar cross-polarization (`VH/VV`) and topographic drainage modeling rather than optical NDVI, plus automated post-storm PMFBY loss evidence packets.
5. **AI Involvement:** Gradient Boosted Decision Trees for lodging probability + SAR change-detection CNN/thresholding for submergence mapping.
6. **Data Requirements:** Sentinel-1 GRD SAR, SRTM 30m DEM, IMD cyclone track archives, AP/Odisha historical disaster loss data.
7. **Technical Feasibility (15 Days):** **Medium.** SAR preprocessing (speckle filtering, terrain correction) is heavier than Sentinel-2 L2A optical bands.
8. **User Benefits:** Helps farmers decide when early harvesting saves ₹15,000+/acre net of drying costs, and accelerates SDRF/PMFBY claims ([BigHaat](https://www.bighaat.com/te/kisan-vedika/blogs/cyclone-arnab-agricultural-losses-government-relief-crop-compensation-farmer-recovery)).
9. **Limitations:** Narrowly focused on extreme storm windows rather than full-season nutrient and irrigation optimization required by the problem prompt.
10. **Demonstration Potential:** Before/after radar replay of the Nov 2026 Cyclone Arnab/Murasu landfall in Kakinada and Prakasam districts.

