### Concept 8: **MicroClimate-PestYield** — Coupled Micro-Weather Disease & Yield Loss Prevention Engine
1. **Project Identity:**
   * **One-Line Description:** Pre-symptomatic epidemiological + satellite red-edge stress engine that predicts fungal/pest outbreaks 7–10 days before visible lesions and quantifies avoidable yield loss.
   * **Main Objective:** Cut preventive broad-spectrum pesticide spraying while preventing the 20–35% yield loss caused by late disease treatment ([ResearchGate Global Agri Vision 2026](https://www.researchgate.net/publication/404936058_Global_Agri_Vision_Artificial_Intelligence_Transforming_Agronomy_with_Predictive_Analytics)).
   * **Primary Target User:** Paddy, wheat, and cotton farmers in humid/irrigated belts.
2. **Real-World Problem:** [Plantix](https://www.mayankdigitallabs.in/blog/ai-crop-disease-detection-farmers-2026) only works *after* a farmer spots lesions and takes a photo; hyperspectral drones cost ₹8–20 lakh ([Mayank Digital Labs](https://www.mayankdigitallabs.in/blog/ai-crop-disease-detection-farmers-2026)).
3. **Proposed Solution:** Combines hourly temperature-humidity-leaf-wetness epidemiological rules (for rice blast, wheat rust, pink bollworm) with 10m/20m Sentinel-2 Red-Edge (`NDRE`) anomalies to flag hotspots before visible spread.
4. **Innovation:** Zero-hardware pre-symptomatic outbreak probability map linked to yield-at-risk calculation.
5. **AI Involvement:** Gradient-boosted epidemiological risk model + spatial anomaly detection on Sentinel-2 Red-Edge bands.
6. **Data Requirements:** Hourly weather (Open-Meteo / NASA POWER), Sentinel-2 Bands 5–8A, ICAR pest weather thresholds.
7. **Technical Feasibility (15 Days):** **Medium.** Ground-truth historical pest outbreak labels at district/plot scale are much harder to obtain publicly than crop yield labels.
8. **User Benefits:** Reduces pesticide spend by ~23% and disease yield loss by ~18% ([CGIAR study cited in Mayank Digital Labs](https://www.mayankdigitallabs.in/blog/ai-crop-disease-detection-farmers-2026)).
9. **Limitations:** Scarcity of open, geo-tagged historical pest-incidence datasets in India makes rigorous ML validation difficult within 15 days.
10. **Demonstration Potential:** Pre-symptomatic rice blast and pink bollworm risk radar overlaid on yield-at-risk estimates.

