### Why Weak Ideas Were Rejected
* **Why Concept 8 (`MicroClimate-PestYield`) is Rejected (#8, Score 3.65):** While disease causes 20–35% crop losses, **there is no clean, public, multi-year plot/district dataset in India mapping daily pest outbreaks to final crop yield**. Building it in 15 days would force the team to rely on synthetic labels, which rigorous technical judges will immediately penalize.
* **Why Concept 2 (`SAR-Shield`) is Not Standalone (#5, Score 4.09):** Processing raw Sentinel-1 GRD radar scenes from scratch is computationally heavy, and focusing *only* on cyclone landfall weeks ignores day-to-day fertilizer and water optimization required by the official problem statement. Instead, we incorporate **pre-computed Sentinel-1 SAR backscatter indices (`VV/VH`) via Google Earth Engine / Copernicus Statistical API** as a cloud-fallback layer inside **Concept 1 (`Pragnya KisanPulse`)**.

