## 3. Deep Comparison Tables for the Top 3 Ideas (Section 7 Requirement)

### 3.1 Top Idea #1: **Pragnya KisanPulse** (Score: 4.71 / 5.00)

| Dimension | Detailed Assessment |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Technical Advantages** | Directly satisfies every word of the prompt (*weather + soil + crop + satellite → yield prediction + resource optimization*). Combines **CatBoost/XGBoost Conformal Quantile Regression** (`P10/P50/P90`) with an agronomic **Counterfactual Timing Solver** (`SAVI` at Day 81 + `NDMI` moisture + 7-day rain leaching physics). |
| **Financial & Farmer Benefits** | Prevents applying ₹1,000–₹1,800/acre of urea right before leaching rains (addressing India's 55–70% N loss per [PIB 2026](https://www.pib.gov.in/PressReleasePage.aspx?PRID=2237709)) and cuts 15–25% unneeded irrigation turns without requiring ₹20,000 IoT sensors. |
| **Innovation Advantages** | Shifts the paradigm from *"What will my yield be?"* to *"What happens to my yield and input waste if I delay irrigation/urea by 4 days?"* Plus native missing-data tolerance (`SparseCast` conformal intervals). |
| **Data Availability & Difficulty** | **High availability / Medium difficulty.** Uses [UPAg](https://upag.gov.in/) / [ICRISAT](https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/ywp3y5j9vv/1) district yield history, [Copernicus Sentinel-1/2](https://dataspace.copernicus.eu/), NASA POWER / Open-Meteo APIs, and [ISRIC SoilGrids](https://un-spider.org/sites/default/files/GeoAI%20Compendium%202026.pdf). |
| **15-Day Dev Time & Infra** | Achievable in 12–14 days by 4 students; runs on standard laptop + free cloud tier (FastAPI + React + pre-extracted GEE/Copernicus tile cache for demo regions). |
| **Adoption & Competition Risks** | Competes conceptually with Fasal and Cropin, but wins on **zero hardware cost** and **plot-level counterfactual ROI**. Main technical risk is district-to-plot label disaggregation, mitigated via explicit `P10–P90` uncertainty intervals. |

* **Why we SHOULD choose Concept 1:** It hits 100% of the judging rubric, solves a verified ₹1,000+/acre pain point using real 2026 Indian data, and gives judges an unforgettable interactive demo (sliding rainfall/urea timing and watching yield vs. waste update live).
* **Why we might NOT choose Concept 1:** It requires integrating 4 distinct data pipelines (weather, soil, satellite indices, yield history), so strict scope discipline is required to finish cleanly in 15 days.

